      "writtenOn": "2017-10-12T21:15:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then do we want to replace this with something like:\n\n\nfunc (c *config) JdkVersions() (javacVersion string, targetVersion string) {\n  envVar :\u003d c.Getenv(\"EXPERIMENTAL_USE_OPENJDK9\")\n  if envVar \u003d\u003d \"\" {\n    return \"1.8\", \"1.8\"\n  }\n  if envVar \u003d\u003d \"true\" {\n    return \"1.9\", \"1.9\"\n  }\n  if envVar \u003d\u003d \"jdk1.8\" {\n    return \"1.9\", \"1.8\"\n  }\n  panic(\"illegal value \u0027\" + envVar + \u0027\")\n}\n\n// Returns true if OpenJDK9 prebuilts are being used\nfunc (c *config) UseOpenJDK9() bool {\n  javacVersion, _ :\u003d c.JdkVersions()\n  return javacVersion\u003d\u003d\"1.9\"\n}\n\n// Returns true if -source 1.9 -target 1.9 is being passed to javac\nfunc (c *config) TargetOpenJDK9() bool {\n  _, targetVersion :\u003d c.JdkVersions()\n  return targetVersion\u003d\u003d\"1.9\"\n}\n?\n\notherwise, for example, setting changing EXPERIMENTAL_USE_OPENJDK9 from \"\" to \"false\" would actually cause javac 9 to be enabled",
